\begin{verbatim}
% RULE Rfinpastsuperdeixis1
< m1:CLAUSE{CLAUSErec1}
           [mu1,
            predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                   [mu2,
                    rel1/VERB{VERBrec1}[mu4],
                    mu3
                   ],
             mu5
           ] 
>

< m :CLAUSE{CLAUSErec2}
           [mu1,
            predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                   [mu2,
                    rel1/VERB{VERBrec2}[mu4],
                    mu3
                   ],
             mu5
           ] 

>
   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
      >

<
   SUBRULE (* no adverbials *)
      <mu5: [I1: mu6]>
      <mu5: [I1: mu6]>

   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I1: QUOTE_temprefnotfound(mu6)
      >

      COMP
         <
          C1:((CLAUSErec1.deixis= omegadeixis) AND
              (CLAUSErec1.aspect <> habitual) AND
              (VERBrec1.tense = omegatense) AND
              (VERBrec1.conjclasses * [13] = []) AND
              (CLAUSErec1.finiteness = finite) AND
              ((CLAUSErec1.aspect <> perfective) OR
               ((CLAUSErec1.aspect = perfective) AND
                (CLAUSErec1.retro = false ->
                 QUOTE_tempdurnotfound(mu5))
               )
              )
             )

             C11:(CLAUSErec1.superdeixis = omegadeixis)
             A11:CLAUSErec2 := CLAUSErec1;
                 CLAUSErec2.superdeixis := pastdeixis;
             
             (* modal + dependent clause *)
             C12:(CLAUSErec1.superdeixis = pastdeixis) 
             A12: CLAUSErec2 := CLAUSErec1;

          A1: VERBrec2 := VERBrec1;
              VERBrec2.tense := pasttense;

         >
      DECOMP
         <
          C1:((VERBrec2.tense = pasttense) AND
              (VERBrec2.conjclasses * [13] = []) AND
              (CLAUSErec2.finiteness = finite) AND
              (CLAUSErec2.aspect <> habitual) AND
              (CLAUSErec2.deixis = omegadeixis) AND
              ((CLAUSErec2.aspect <> perfective) OR
               ((CLAUSErec2.aspect = perfective) AND
                (CLAUSErec2.retro = false ->
                 QUOTE_tempdurnotfound(mu5))
               )
              )
             )
              C11: (CLAUSErec2.superdeixis = pastdeixis)
              A11: CLAUSErec1 := CLAUSErec2;
                   CLAUSErec1.superdeixis := omegadeixis;

             (* modal + dependent clause *)
              C12: (CLAUSErec2.superdeixis = pastdeixis)
              A12: CLAUSErec1 := CLAUSErec2;
 
          A1: VERBrec1 := VERBrec2;
              VERBrec1.tense := omegatense;

         >



>
&

\end{verbatim}
\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] Rfinpastsuperdeixis1
\item[* relevant examples:] he said that he worked,
he said that he could....,
he said that he would.....,
he said that he was ill,
he said that he was working,
he said that he had worked (for 4 hours),
*he said that he worked for 4 hours,
*he said that he `musted'
\item[* language:] English
\item[* kind of rule:] M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] XPPROPtoCLAUSE
\item[* class:] Deixis rules
\item[* date of creation:] 28-MAR-1988 
\item[* author:] Lisette Appelo
\item[* copied from:] Rfinpresentsuperdeixis 
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 19/05/89\ \ \ \ \ author: Lisette Appelo\\
Splitted Rfinpastsuperdeixis into Rfinpastsuperdeixis1 and Rfinpastsuperdeixis2
. This rule does not allow for reference adverbials and it corresponds to 
Lpastsuperdeixis and has the same semantics as Rinfinpastsuperdeixis. 
\item date: 23/06/89\ \ \ \ \ author: Lisette Appelo\\
Added conditions on perfective, non-retro aspect with a duration adverbial. 
This case should be handled by Rfinpastsuperdeixis2. 
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] The relation between Rs and S is before : PAST.
               This rule is for a finite dependent clause.
               The most left verb in the clause gets a past tense.
               The deixis 
value of the possible reference adverbial is checked for 
               omega.
               The clause is marked for past superdeixis.
\item[\ \ strategy:] The match is supposed to be left to right.
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:] The splitting into
subrules corresponds to the different categories of the variables for the 
reference adverbials. 
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
\item[\ \ differences analytical/generative version:]
\item[\  \ suggested semantics:] function application (see task)
\item[\ \ presuppositions:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item dictionary:\\

\item rules: finiteness transformations, rules that introduce the 
reference adverbial \\

\end{enumerate}
\item[\ \ consequences in the grammar:]
\item[\ \ translation aspects:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate} 
\item within this language:\\

\item in other languages:\\

\end{enumerate}
\item[* relevant literature/documents:] doc 53, 263, 314, 320.
\item[\ \ remarks:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item problems:\\

\item modifications: The superdeixis value also may be pastdeixis in the case 
this sentence is a sentence with adverbs such as {\em graag} in Dutch. 
In English this may be 
the case in cases in which e.g. a verb is a semantic head but behaves as an  
auxiliary verb (e.g. modal verbs)\\

\end{enumerate}
\end{description}

\newpage
\begin{verbatim}
% RULE Rfinpastsuperdeixis2
< m1:CLAUSE{CLAUSErec1}
           [mu1,
            predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                   [mu2,
                    rel1/VERB{VERBrec1}[mu4],
                    mu3
                   ],
             mu5
           ] 
>

< m :CLAUSE{CLAUSErec2}
           [mu1,
            predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                   [mu2,
                    rel1/VERB{VERBrec2}[mu4],
                    mu3
                   ],
             mu5
           ] 

>
   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
      >

<


   SUBRULE (* 1: duration adverbial, no referential adverbial *)
      <mu5: [I1: mu6]>
      <mu5: [I1: mu6]>

   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I1: (QUOTE_temprefnotfound(mu6)) AND
           (NOT (QUOTE_tempdurnotfound(mu6)))
       >

      COMP
         <
          C1:((CLAUSErec1.deixis= omegadeixis) AND
              (CLAUSErec1.aspect <> habitual) AND
              (VERBrec1.tense = omegatense) AND
              (VERBrec1.conjclasses * [13] = []) AND
              (CLAUSErec1.finiteness = finite)
             )

             C11:(CLAUSErec1.superdeixis = omegadeixis)
             A11:CLAUSErec2 := CLAUSErec1;
                 CLAUSErec2.superdeixis := pastdeixis;
             
             (* modal + dependent clause *)
             C12:(CLAUSErec1.superdeixis = pastdeixis)
             A12: CLAUSErec2 := CLAUSErec1;

          A1: VERBrec2 := VERBrec1;
              VERBrec2.tense := pasttense;

         >
      DECOMP
         <
          C1:((VERBrec2.tense = pasttense) AND
              (VERBrec2.conjclasses * [13] = []) AND
              (CLAUSErec2.finiteness = finite) AND
              (CLAUSErec2.aspect <> habitual) AND
              (CLAUSErec2.deixis = omegadeixis)
             )
              C11: (CLAUSErec2.superdeixis = pastdeixis)
              A11: CLAUSErec1 := CLAUSErec2;
                   CLAUSErec1.superdeixis := omegadeixis;

             (* modal + dependent clause *)
              C12: (CLAUSErec2.superdeixis = pastdeixis)
              A12: CLAUSErec1 := CLAUSErec2;
 
          A1: VERBrec1 := VERBrec2;
              VERBrec1.tense := omegatense;

         >

   SUBRULE (* 2: ADVPVAR *)
      <mu5: [I1: mu6, I2:tempadvrel/ADVPVAR{ADVPVARrec1}[ ], I3: mu7]>
      <mu5: [I1: mu6, I2:tempadvrel/ADVPVAR{ADVPVARrec1}[ ], I3: mu7]>

   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I1: QUOTE_temprefnotfound(mu6)
       I2: ((ADVPVARrec1.class = reference) AND
            (ADVPVARrec1.retro = false) AND
            (ADVPVARrec1.deixis IN [omegadeixis,pastdeixis])
           )
       I3: QUOTE_temprefnotfound(mu7)
      >

      COMP
         <
          C1:((CLAUSErec1.deixis= omegadeixis) AND
              (CLAUSErec1.aspect <> habitual) AND
              (VERBrec1.tense = omegatense) AND
              (VERBrec1.conjclasses * [13] = []) AND
              (CLAUSErec1.finiteness = finite)
             )

             C11:(CLAUSErec1.superdeixis = omegadeixis)
             A11:CLAUSErec2 := CLAUSErec1;
                 CLAUSErec2.superdeixis := pastdeixis;
             
             (* modal + dependent clause *)
             C12:(CLAUSErec1.superdeixis = pastdeixis)
             A12: CLAUSErec2 := CLAUSErec1;

          A1: VERBrec2 := VERBrec1;
              VERBrec2.tense := pasttense;

         >
      DECOMP
         <
          C1:((VERBrec2.tense = pasttense) AND
              (VERBrec2.conjclasses * [13] = []) AND
              (CLAUSErec2.finiteness = finite) AND
              (CLAUSErec2.aspect <> habitual) AND
              (CLAUSErec2.deixis = omegadeixis)
             )
              C11: (CLAUSErec2.superdeixis = pastdeixis)
              A11: CLAUSErec1 := CLAUSErec2;
                   CLAUSErec1.superdeixis := omegadeixis;

             (* modal + dependent clause *)
              C12: (CLAUSErec2.superdeixis = pastdeixis)
              A12: CLAUSErec1 := CLAUSErec2;
 
          A1: VERBrec1 := VERBrec2;
              VERBrec1.tense := omegatense;

         >


   SUBRULE (* 3: PREPPVAR *)
      <mu5: [I1: mu6, I2: tempadvrel/PREPPVAR{PREPPVARrec1}[ ], I3: mu7]>
      <mu5: [I1: mu6, I2: tempadvrel/PREPPVAR{PREPPVARrec1}[ ], I3: mu7]>

   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I1: QUOTE_temprefnotfound(mu6)
       I2: ((PREPPVARrec1.class = reference) AND
            (PREPPVARrec1.retro = false) AND
            (PREPPVARrec1.deixis IN [omegadeixis, pastdeixis])
           )
       I3: QUOTE_temprefnotfound(mu7)
      >

      COMP
         <
          C1:((CLAUSErec1.deixis= omegadeixis) AND
              (CLAUSErec1.aspect <> habitual) AND
              (VERBrec1.tense = omegatense) AND
              (VERBrec1.conjclasses * [13] = []) AND
              (CLAUSErec1.finiteness = finite)
             )

             C11:(CLAUSErec1.superdeixis = omegadeixis)
             A11:CLAUSErec2 := CLAUSErec1;
                 CLAUSErec2.superdeixis := pastdeixis;
             
             (* modal + dependent clause *)
             C12:(CLAUSErec1.superdeixis = pastdeixis)
             A12: CLAUSErec2 := CLAUSErec1;

          A1: VERBrec2 := VERBrec1;
              VERBrec2.tense := pasttense;

         >
      DECOMP
         <
          C1:((VERBrec2.tense = pasttense) AND
              (VERBrec2.conjclasses * [13] = []) AND
              (CLAUSErec2.finiteness = finite) AND
              (CLAUSErec2.aspect <> habitual) AND
              (CLAUSErec2.deixis = omegadeixis)
             )
              C11: (CLAUSErec2.superdeixis = pastdeixis)
              A11: CLAUSErec1 := CLAUSErec2;
                   CLAUSErec1.superdeixis := omegadeixis;

             (* modal + dependent clause *)
              C12: (CLAUSErec2.superdeixis = pastdeixis)
              A12: CLAUSErec1 := CLAUSErec2;
 
          A1: VERBrec1 := VERBrec2;
              VERBrec1.tense := omegatense;

         >


   SUBRULE (* 4: SENTENCE *)
      <mu5: [I1:mu6, I2: tempadvrel/SENTENCE{SENTENCErec1}[mu9], I3:mu7]>
      <mu5: [I1:mu6, I2: tempadvrel/SENTENCE{SENTENCErec1}[mu9], I3:mu7]>

   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I1: QUOTE_temprefnotfound(mu6)
       I2: ((SENTENCErec1.conjclass = reference) AND
            (SENTENCErec1.conjretro = false) AND
            (SENTENCErec1.conjdeixis IN [omegadeixis, pastdeixis]) AND
            (SENTENCErec1.temporal = true)
           )
       I3: QUOTE_temprefnotfound(mu7)

      >

      COMP
         <
          C1:((CLAUSErec1.deixis= omegadeixis) AND
              (CLAUSErec1.aspect <> habitual) AND
              (VERBrec1.tense = omegatense) AND
              (VERBrec1.conjclasses * [13] = []) AND
              (CLAUSErec1.finiteness = finite)
             )

             C11:(CLAUSErec1.superdeixis = omegadeixis)
             A11:CLAUSErec2 := CLAUSErec1;
                 CLAUSErec2.superdeixis := pastdeixis;
             
             (* modal + dependent clause *)
             C12:(CLAUSErec1.superdeixis = pastdeixis) 
             A12: CLAUSErec2 := CLAUSErec1;

          A1: VERBrec2 := VERBrec1;
              VERBrec2.tense := pasttense;

         >
      DECOMP
         <
          C1:((VERBrec2.tense = pasttense) AND
              (VERBrec2.conjclasses * [13] = []) AND
              (CLAUSErec2.finiteness = finite) AND
              (CLAUSErec2.aspect <> habitual) AND
              (CLAUSErec2.deixis = omegadeixis)
             )
              C11: (CLAUSErec2.superdeixis = pastdeixis)
              A11: CLAUSErec1 := CLAUSErec2;
                   CLAUSErec1.superdeixis := omegadeixis;

             (* modal + dependent clause *)
              C12: (CLAUSErec2.superdeixis = pastdeixis)
              A12: CLAUSErec1 := CLAUSErec2;
 
          A1: VERBrec1 := VERBrec2;
              VERBrec1.tense := omegatense;

         >

>
&

\end{verbatim}
\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] Rfinpastsuperdeixis2
\item[* relevant examples:] he said that he worked at 3 o'clock,
he said that he could....at 3 o'clock,
he said that he would.....at 3 o'clock,
he said that he was ill at 3 o'clock,
he said that he was working at 3 o'clock,
he said that he worked for 4 hours,
*he said that he `musted'at 3 o'clock
\item[* language:] English
\item[* kind of rule:] M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] XPPROPtoCLAUSE
\item[* class:] Deixis rules
\item[* date of creation:] 28-MAR-1988 
\item[* author:] Lisette Appelo
\item[* copied from:] Rfinpastsuperdeixis1 
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 19/05/89\ \ \ \ \ author: Lisette Appelo\\
Splitted Rfinpastsuperdeixis into Rfinpastsuperdeixis1 and Rfinpastsuperdeixis2
. This rule requires a reference adverbial and corresponds to 
Lpastpastsuperdeixis. This means that it has the same semantics as 
Rinfinpastsuperdeixis. 
\item date: 01/06/89\ \ \ \ \ author: Lisette Appelo\\
Added pastdeixis to condition on adverbial to be able to translate {\em Hij zie 
dat hij gisteren had gezwommen} into {\em He said that he swam yesterday}
\item date: 23/06/89\ \ \ \ \ author: Lisette Appelo\\
Added first subrule that accounts for the case in which a referential advebial 
is absent, but a durational adverbial is present: {\em He said that he swam for 
4 hours} in a `past-past'-interpretration.
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] The relation between Rs and S is before : PAST.
               This rule is for a finite dependent clause.
               The most left verb in the clause gets a past tense.
               The deixis 
value of the possible reference adverbial is checked for 
               omega.
               The clause is marked for past superdeixis.
\item[\ \ strategy:] The match is supposed to be left to right.
